# drf-react-by-schema-agent-console

Themeable **Agent Console** chat UI for [drf-react-by-schema](https://www.npmjs.com/package/drf-react-by-schema) apps. A React/MUI panel over a
per-user **opencode** instance brokered by the host's Django backend, built on
`@assistant-ui/react`.

## Overview

The package renders a chat over an agent defined in the project's `opencode.json`. The
browser never talks to opencode directly: it hits the host's admin-gated Django **broker**,
which mints/reuses the caller's OAuth token and proxies to the instance. The host's SimpleJWT
(`localStorage.token` by default) is injected into every request, REST and SSE alike.

Two entry points:

- `AgentConsole` — the bare panel (session list, message thread, composer, markdown, tool
  cards, copy/download reply actions, mobile sessions drawer). No page chrome, no gate.
- `AgentPage` — the full page: an auth gate (`canUseAssistant`), a page shell
  (`renderShell`) and the panel.

The package is deliberately **dependency-light**: it does **not** import
`drf-react-by-schema`. The host passes `usuaria`, `isMobile`, the gate, texts, styles
and (optionally) slots/shell.

## Installation

```bash
npm install drf-react-by-schema-agent-console
```

The following are **peer dependencies** and must be installed by the host (they become part
of the app bundle and must be shared with it):

`@assistant-ui/react ^0.15.28`, `@assistant-ui/react-markdown ^0.14.21`,
`@assistant-ui/react-opencode ^0.2.31`, `remark-gfm ^4`, `@mui/material ^6`,
`@mui/icons-material ^6`, `react ^19`, `react-dom ^19`.

## Usage

Full page (the common case):

```tsx
import { AgentPage } from 'drf-react-by-schema-agent-console';
import { useAPIWrapper } from 'drf-react-by-schema';

function AssistentePage() {
  const { usuaria, isMobile } = useAPIWrapper();
  return (
    <AgentPage
      brokerUrl={`${API_URL}/agent-console`}
      agent="myapp-console"
      usuaria={usuaria}
      canUseAssistant={(u) => !!u?.is_superuser}
      isMobile={isMobile}
      texts={{
        emptyTitle: 'Assistente',
        composerPlaceholder: 'Pergunte sobre os dados…',
      }}
      renderShell={PageShell}
    />
  );
}
```

Bare panel (inside your own layout):

```tsx
import { AgentConsole } from 'drf-react-by-schema-agent-console';

<AgentConsole brokerUrl={`${API_URL}/agent-console`} agent="myapp-console" />;
```

## Theming

There are **no hardcoded colors**. The defaults come from `buildDefaultStyles(theme, {
brandColor })`, where every value is a MUI theme token or `brandColor` (default
`theme.palette.primary.main`). A host re-themes entirely through its MUI theme, and can
override a subset by deep-merging the `styles` prop:

```tsx
import { buildDefaultStyles } from 'drf-react-by-schema-agent-console/styles';

<AgentConsole
  brokerUrl={brokerUrl}
  agent="myapp-console"
  brandColor="#0d6efd"
  styles={{ responseCard: { borderRadius: 4 } }}
/>;
```

The full prop / texts / styles / slots reference lives in
[docs/API_REFERENCE.md](docs/API_REFERENCE.md).

